{"id": "unknown-2026-06-04-008", "date": "2026-06-04", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solar streetlights with AI could solve data center energy demand", "content": "<p>Putting Nvidia computer chips into solar-powered streetlamps to create a virtual power plant is a simple solution to the energy demand problems created by data centers, according to Edward Fitzgerald. His company ConFlow Power Group is doing exactly that with its iLamp streetlamps, he told pv magazine.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/solar-streetlights-with-ai-nvidia-chips-could-solve-data-center-energy-demand-green-utilities-conflow-power-group/\">Solar streetl", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/solar-streetlights-with-ai-nvidia-chips-could-solve-data-center-energy-demand-green-utilities-conflow-power-group/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-04-009", "date": "2026-06-04", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["concerns"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "European Commission to conduct risk assessment of EU solar, wind installations", "content": "<p>The European Commission says its new strategic roadmap for digitalization and AI in energy will address cybersecurity concerns by undertaking a risk assessment of solar and wind installations in the EU and reviewing the energy security of supply framework.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/european-commission-to-conduct-risk-assessment-of-eu-solar-wind-installations/\">European Commission to conduct risk assessment of EU solar, wind installations</a> appeared firs", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/european-commission-to-conduct-risk-assessment-of-eu-solar-wind-installations/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-04-010", "date": "2026-06-04", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["trade_tariff", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India extends countervailing duty on Malaysian solar glass imports for five years", "content": "<p>The move follows a recommendation from India's Directorate General of Trade Remedies, which found that removing the duty would likely lead to the continuation or recurrence of subsidized imports and material injury to domestic manufacturers.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/india-extends-countervailing-duty-on-malaysian-solar-glass-imports-for-five-years/\">India extends countervailing duty on Malaysian solar glass imports for five years</a> appeared first on <a ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/india-extends-countervailing-duty-on-malaysian-solar-glass-imports-for-five-years/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-04-011", "date": "2026-06-04", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "UK hits 22.3 GW solar capacity as cost per kW falls", "content": "<p>Latest government data records 2,026,000 installations totaling 22.3 GW of capacity. Total installed capacity grew by 11.2% over the 12 months to the end of April 2026.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/uk-hits-22-3-gw-solar-capacity-as-cost-per-kw-falls/\">UK hits 22.3 GW solar capacity as cost per kW falls</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/uk-hits-22-3-gw-solar-capacity-as-cost-per-kw-falls/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-04-012", "date": "2026-06-04", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Mauritius tenders 220 MW of solar and storage via new ‘e-Marketplace’", "content": "<p>Mauritius has published tenders for solar plus storage projects totalling 220 MW. The tender is launched on a new E-Marketplace created by the International Solar Alliance, which aims to improve bankability and access to finance for projects in small island developing states (SIDS).</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/mauritius-tenders-220-mw-of-solar-and-storage-via-new-e-marketplace/\">Mauritius tenders 220 MW of solar and storage via new ‘e-Marketplace’</a> appea", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/mauritius-tenders-220-mw-of-solar-and-storage-via-new-e-marketplace/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-04-013", "date": "2026-06-04", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Hybrid solar-hydrogen project planned at Antarctic base", "content": "<p>A hybrid power pilot project combining solar, batteries and hydrogen fuel cells is under development at a scientific base on King George Island to explore reducing diesel consumption in isolated research operations.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/giz-valida-un-piloto-de-energias-renovables-e-hidrogeno-en-una-base-antartica-chilena/\">Hybrid solar-hydrogen project planned at Antarctic base</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine G", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/giz-valida-un-piloto-de-energias-renovables-e-hidrogeno-en-una-base-antartica-chilena/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-04-014", "date": "2026-06-04", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 23, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Queensland opens funding call for solar, wind, storage projects", "content": "<p>The government of Queensland in Australia is calling for industry proposals to deliver new solar, wind and battery storage projects with the backing of an AUD 200 million ($144 million) fund.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/queensland-seeks-new-energy-generation-and-storage-proposals-under-200-million-fund/\">Queensland opens funding call for solar, wind, storage projects</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/04/queensland-seeks-new-energy-generation-and-storage-proposals-under-200-million-fund/", "type": "rss"}]}
